  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [800-01, 800-02, 800-03, Planning, Heritage, Design and Access Statement, 351 00 00, 351 00 10, 351 00 20, 351 00 21, Planning Fire Safety Strategy, Flood Risk Matrix, 351 38 00, 351 38 10, 351 38 20, 351 38 21, Arboricultural survey and constraints received 22/06/2026].\r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The detached single storey outbuilding hereby permitted shall only be used for a purpose incidental to the enjoyment of the house at the '1A Bath Road, Chiswick, W4 1LL' described at the top of this decision letter and for no other purpose (for example, it may not be used as a self-contained dwelling or contain a bedroom, bathroom, kitchen or other primary residential accommodation, nor may it be used for business purposes). \r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' living conditions and the character of the area.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The trees that are specified on the Planning, Heritage, Design and Access Statement and Arboricultural Survey and Constraints hereby approved to be retained shall be protected before commencement of any works on site and throughout the course of the development by methods that conform to the best practice guidance contained in British Standard BS5837: 2012 or any guidance that shall have superseded it\r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure a satisfactory appearance of the site and the area and to promote biodiversity."
